### ─── Supplier management endpoints (PMS-011) ──────────────────────────────────
### Uses the REST Client extension (humao.rest-client).
### Covers `POST /api/suppliers`, `GET /api/suppliers`,
### `GET /api/suppliers/search`, `GET /api/suppliers/:id`,
### `PATCH /api/suppliers/:id`, `PATCH /api/suppliers/:id/deactivate`,
### and `PATCH /api/suppliers/:id/activate`.
###
### Roles: only ADMIN and PHARMACIST may use supplier endpoints.
### CASHIER requests are rejected with 403.
###
### Soft-delete policy:
###   Suppliers are NEVER physically deleted. `deactivate` flips `active=false`
###   so historical purchase_orders keep a valid reference. There is no DELETE
###   route. Reactivate a supplier with the `activate` route (or PATCH with
###   `active: true`).
###
### NIT rule:
###   The NIT is a tax id stored as DIGITS ONLY. Any non-digit character is
###   stripped before validation/persistence ("123-456-789" → "123456789").
###   It is globally unique: reusing an existing NIT returns 409 DUPLICATE_NIT,
###   even for a deactivated supplier.
###
### Quick start:
###   1. Start the API:  npm start
###   2. Send the "LOGIN as pharmacist" and "LOGIN as admin" requests below.
###   3. Walk through the create → search → deactivate → activate flow.

@host = http://localhost
@port = 3000
@base = {{host}}:{{port}}/api


### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### AUTH — log in as a pharmacist, an admin, and a cashier (used to prove the
### cashier role is rejected).
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# @name loginPharmacist
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "email": "pharmacist@openpharmacy.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### ── Login as Admin ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# @name loginAdmin
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@openpharmacy.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### ── Login as Cashier ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# @name loginCashier
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "email": "cashier@openpharmacy.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### ── Store tokens for later requests ─────────────────────────────────────────
@pharmToken = {{loginPharmacist.response.body.accessToken}}
@adminToken = {{loginAdmin.response.body.accessToken}}
@cashierToken = {{loginCashier.response.body.accessToken}}


### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### 1. CREATE SUPPLIER — pharmacist creates a new supplier.
###    Expect: 201 with the created supplier (active=true).
###    NOTE the formatted NIT "900-456-789": it is stored as "900456789".
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# @name createSupplier
POST {{base}}/suppliers
Authorization: Bearer {{pharmToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Distribuidora Farmacéutica Nacional",
  "nit": "900-456-789",
  "address": "Av. Juan Pablo II 123",
  "city": "La Paz",
  "contact_person": "Ana Lopez",
  "phone": "+591 70012345",
  "email": "ventas@dfn.example.com",
  "payment_terms": "Net 30"
}

### ── The id of the supplier we just created, reused below ────────────────────
@supplierId = {{createSupplier.response.body.id}}


### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### 2. LIST ACTIVE SUPPLIERS — the lightweight dropdown endpoint.
###    Returns only active suppliers, sorted by name.
###    Expect: 200 + [ { id, name, nit, active: true, ... }, ... ]
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

GET {{base}}/suppliers
Authorization: Bearer {{pharmToken}}


### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### 3. SEARCH SUPPLIERS — paginated, filterable admin list.
###    Query params: q (name / nit / contact), active, page, pageSize (max 200).
###    Expect: 200 + { data, total, page, pageSize, totalPages }.
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

GET {{base}}/suppliers/search?q=Farma&page=1&pageSize=20
Authorization: Bearer {{pharmToken}}

### ── Include deactivated suppliers in the search ─────────────────────────────
GET {{base}}/suppliers/search?active=false&page=1&pageSize=20
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### 4. GET SUPPLIER BY ID — includes deactivated suppliers.
###    Expect: 200 + supplier.
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

GET {{base}}/suppliers/{{supplierId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### 5. UPDATE SUPPLIER — partial update.
###    Expect: 200 + updated supplier.
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

PATCH {{base}}/suppliers/{{supplierId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{pharmToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phone": "+591 71111111",
  "payment_terms": "Net 45"
}


### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### 6. DEACTIVATE SUPPLIER — soft delete (active=false).
###    Historical purchase orders are preserved.
###    Expect: 200 + supplier with active=false.
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

PATCH {{base}}/suppliers/{{supplierId}}/deactivate
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### ── It now disappears from the active dropdown list ─────────────────────────
GET {{base}}/suppliers
Authorization: Bearer {{pharmToken}}

### ── ...but is still retrievable by id ───────────────────────────────────────
GET {{base}}/suppliers/{{supplierId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### 7. ACTIVATE SUPPLIER — restore a deactivated supplier.
###    Expect: 200 + supplier with active=true.
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

PATCH {{base}}/suppliers/{{supplierId}}/activate
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### 8. NEGATIVE — duplicate NIT returns 409 DUPLICATE_NIT.
###     Re-uses the same digits-only NIT as request #1 above.
###     Expect: 409 with code "DUPLICATE_NIT".
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

POST {{base}}/suppliers
Authorization: Bearer {{pharmToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Duplicate NIT Attempt",
  "nit": "900456789"
}


### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### 9. NEGATIVE — a NIT with no digits is rejected.
###     "abc-def" normalizes to an empty string, which fails validation.
###     Expect: 400 from ValidationPipe (nit must contain at least one digit).
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

POST {{base}}/suppliers
Authorization: Bearer {{pharmToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "No Digits Supplier",
  "nit": "abc-def"
}


### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### 10. NEGATIVE — a cashier cannot manage suppliers.
###     Expect: 403 from the RolesGuard.
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

POST {{base}}/suppliers
Authorization: Bearer {{cashierToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Cashier Attempt",
  "nit": "900999000"
}


### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### 11. NEGATIVE — get an unknown supplier id.
###     Expect: 404.
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

GET {{base}}/suppliers/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### 12. PURCHASE-ORDER INTEGRATION — reuse the active-supplier dropdown, then
###     draft a PO against a supplier returned by GET /api/suppliers.
###     Replace SUPPLIER_UUID / PRODUCT_UUID with real values from the list
###     endpoints. Deactivated suppliers are NOT selectable here.
###     Expect: 201 PENDING purchase order.
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

GET {{base}}/suppliers
Authorization: Bearer {{pharmToken}}

###
POST {{base}}/purchase-orders
Authorization: Bearer {{pharmToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "supplierId": "SUPPLIER_UUID",
  "orderDate": "2026-09-20",
  "items": [
    {
      "productId": "PRODUCT_UUID",
      "qtyOrdered": 50,
      "unitCost": 8.50
    }
  ]
}


### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### 13. NEGATIVE — a PO against a deactivated supplier is rejected.
###     First deactivate a supplier (request #6), then try to order from it.
###     Expect: 400 with code "SUPPLIER_INACTIVE".
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

POST {{base}}/purchase-orders
Authorization: Bearer {{pharmToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "supplierId": "{{supplierId}}",
  "orderDate": "2026-09-20",
  "items": [
    {
      "productId": "PRODUCT_UUID",
      "qtyOrdered": 10,
      "unitCost": 8.50
    }
  ]
}
